Markdown Content:
{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":116601,"name":"Daisuke Kato","username":"Daisuke_Kato","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/daisuke_kato/{size}/23487_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-08T14:30:45.695Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI have been looking into \u003ccode\u003erosidl::Buffer\u003c/code\u003e and the current buffer backend support, particularly for large variable-length payloads such as images and point clouds.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne idea I am interested in is a CPU shared-memory backend for \u003ccode\u003erosidl::Buffer\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI realize that this overlaps to some extent with functionality that already exists at lower layers. For example, some middleware / RMW implementations already provide shared-memory transport or other zero-copy optimizations. Depending on the implementation, moving data through shared memory may therefore already be possible without introducing a dedicated Buffer backend.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I am trying to understand is whether there is still a useful role for shared memory at the \u003ccode\u003erosidl::Buffer\u003c/code\u003e layer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy interest is specifically in large variable-length fields where avoiding copies of the payload itself is useful. Rather than treating shared memory only as a transport optimization for a serialized message, a Buffer backend could potentially make the payload storage itself shared and let a buffer-aware RMW transport a descriptor or reference when appropriate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConceptually:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eROS message\n  metadata\n  rosidl::Buffer\u0026lt;uint8_t\u0026gt;\n          |\n          +-- CPU shared-memory backend\n                  |\n                  +-- shared payload storage\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis seems potentially complementary to transport-level shared memory rather than necessarily a replacement for it. On the other hand, I can also imagine that the overlap with middleware-native SHM mechanisms may be a reason why such a backend has not been pursued.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn particular, I would be interested in hearing:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHas anyone already explored a CPU shared-memory backend for \u003ccode\u003erosidl::Buffer\u003c/code\u003e?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIs sharing the backing storage of large variable-length payloads considered an intended use of the Buffer backend abstraction?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore prototyping something in this direction, I wanted to check whether there is already related work or design discussion that I have missed. I previously explored a similar problem for CUDA IPC in \u003ca href=\"https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros2-cuda-ipc-zero-copy-gpu-data-sharing-between-ros-2-processes/57157/9\"\u003ethis discussion\u003c/a\u003e, so I would especially like to avoid independently reimplementing something that is already being worked on elsewhere.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-116601-related-links-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-116601-related-links-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eRelated links\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-pmc-minutes-for-july-21-2026/56999\"\u003eROS PMC minutes for July 21, 2026\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e“Qualcomm is working on a buffer implementation, which would be the first non-NVIDIA one”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros2-cuda-ipc-zero-copy-gpu-data-sharing-between-ros-2-processes/57157/9\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eros2_cuda_ipc: Zero-copy GPU data sharing between ROS 2 processes - #9 by ZhenshengLee\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-08-08T14:38:48.430Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":20,"reads":79,"readers_count":78,"score":235.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":57240,"topic_slug":"has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored","display_username":"Daisuke Kato","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros2-cuda-ipc-zero-copy-gpu-data-sharing-between-ros-2-processes/57157/9","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"ros2_cuda_ipc: Zero-copy GPU data sharing between ROS 2 processes","clicks":6},{"url":"https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-pmc-minutes-for-july-21-2026/56999","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"ROS PMC Minutes for July 21, 2026","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":6}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":29837,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored/57240/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":6}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":6,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_vote":false},{"id":116624,"name":"Martin Pecka","username":"peci1","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/peci1/{size}/10145_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-09T16:17:29.793Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHave you answered to the correct topic? I don’t see how is your answer relevant to this one…\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-08-09T16:17:29.793Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":67,"readers_count":66,"score":28.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":57240,"topic_slug":"has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored","display_username":"Martin Pecka","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Great contributor","title_is_group":false,"reply_to_user":{"id":20779,"username":"ZhenshengLee","name":"VictorLee","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/zhenshenglee/{size}/10103_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":5103,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"user_status":{"description":"Czech Technical University in Prague","emoji":"czechia","ends_at":null,"message_bus_last_id":0},"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored/57240/3","reactions":[{"id":"laughing","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":116701,"name":"Daisuke Kato","username":"Daisuke_Kato","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/daisuke_kato/{size}/23487_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-11T13:52:47.519Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eWhile working on this feature, I noticed that pub/sub message delivery time increases roughly in proportion to the buffer size, even though the payload size is expected to remain constant when using specialized buffer backends.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI looked into it a bit and found that \u003ccode\u003estd::vector\u0026lt;uint8_t\u0026gt;(buffer_size)\u003c/code\u003e zero-initializes the entire buffer, effectively calling \u003ccode\u003ememset\u003c/code\u003e for \u003ccode\u003ebuffer_size\u003c/code\u003e bytes. Since the buffer does not need to be initialized in this context, I submitted a patch to avoid both the extra memory allocation and the zero-initialization.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox githubpullrequest\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003egithub.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"github-row\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\"\u003e\n\n\n\n    \u003cdiv class=\"github-icon-container\" title=\"プルリクエスト\"\u003e\n      \u003csvg width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"github-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M11 11.28V5c-.03-.78-.34-1.47-.94-2.06C9.46 2.35 8.78 2.03 8 2H7V0L4 3l3 3V4h1c.27.02.48.11.69.31.21.2.3.42.31.69v6.28A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 10 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72zm-1 2.92c-.66 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2zM4 3c0-1.11-.89-2-2-2a1.993 1.993 0 0 0-1 3.72v6.56A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 2 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72V4.72c.59-.34 1-.98 1-1.72zm-.8 10c0 .66-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2-.65 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2zM2 4.2C1.34 4.2.8 3.65.8 3c0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"github-info-container\"\u003e\n\n\n\n      \u003ch4\u003e\n        \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eReuse FastBuffer managed buffer for each endpoint. (#904)\u003c/a\u003e\n      \u003c/h4\u003e\n\n    \u003cdiv class=\"branches\"\u003e\n      \u003ccode\u003erolling\u003c/code\u003e ← \u003ccode\u003edskkato:dskkato/reduce_extra_heap_allocations\u003c/code\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\n      \u003cdiv class=\"github-info\"\u003e\n        \u003cdiv class=\"date\"\u003e\n          オープン \u003cspan class=\"discourse-local-date\" data-format=\"ll\" data-date=\"2026-08-11\" data-time=\"08:24:48\" data-timezone=\"UTC\"\u003e08:24AM - 11 Aug 26 UTC\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n\n        \u003cdiv class=\"user\"\u003e\n          \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/dskkato\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\n            \u003cimg alt=\"\" src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/f/6/f6e0cc9bb89035f8a510335c29c5eeac271bcf06.jpeg\" class=\"onebox-avatar-inline\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" data-dominant-color=\"919471\"\u003e\n            dskkato\n          \u003c/a\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n\n        \u003cdiv class=\"lines\" title=\"1 個のコミットにより 1 個のファイルが変更されました。12 個が追加され、6 個が削除されました。\"\u003e\n          \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904/files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"added\"\u003e+12\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"removed\"\u003e-6\u003c/span\u003e\n          \u003c/a\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n      \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"github-row\"\u003e\n    \u003cp class=\"github-body-container\"\u003e## Description\n\nPreviously, heap allocation happend for each endpoint with std\u003cspan class=\"show-more-container\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\" class=\"show-more\"\u003e…\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"excerpt hidden\"\u003e::vector\u0026lt;uint8_t\u0026gt;. This introduced extra memset via its constructor.\n\nFor recent ROS 2, where rosidl::Buffer was introduced, sometimes the actual payload size and message size may not match because only buffer descriptors may be sent. In such a case, now `get_serialized_size()` seems to be unreliable, and hard to pre-allocate the buffer in that path.\n\nFixes #903\n\n### Is this user-facing behavior change?\n\n\n\nPossibly yes.\n\nPreviously, it is guaranteed that the heap allocation only happens once per endpoint, through externally managed buffer (allocated with `std::vector\u0026lt;uint8_t\u0026gt;`). Now the number of allocations depends on combinations of buffer's strategies, and Cdr's usage. So, in small message cases, this patch will introduce an extra overhead of buffer reallocation.\n\nFor rosidl::Buffer usage, this patch will dramatically reduce extra allocation and zero-initialization when only the optimized message paths exist. \n\n### Did you use Generative AI?\n\nI used CodeX to investigate the cause analysis, and FastBuffer/Cdr behavior.\n\n### Additional Information\n\nThis patch is trying to resolve two issues at same time:\n\n1. Reducing extra memory allocation when publishing rosidl::Buffer via optimized buf (carries only a descriptor) \n2. Removing extra memset caused by `std::vector\u0026lt;uint8_t\u0026gt;` constructor.\n\nWhat I originally found is the second point, so if we wish more conservative way, it is possible to reserve the `fast_buffer` as previouslly. Still, I believe it is better to reuse that buffer accross endpoints, in my perspective...\n\nSince this is my first PR to `rmw_fastrtps` repository, let me know if I missed anything.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-08-11T13:52:47.519Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":56,"readers_count":55,"score":16.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":57240,"topic_slug":"has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored","display_username":"Daisuke Kato","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Reuse FastBuffer managed buffer for each endpoint. by dskkato · Pull Request #904 · ros2/rmw_fastrtps · GitHub","clicks":8},{"url":"https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/ros-news-for-the-week-of-august-10th-2026/57415","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"ROS News for the week of August 10th, 2026","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":29837,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored/57240/4","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":116714,"name":"Tully Foote","username":"tfoote","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/tfoote/{size}/3813_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-11T16:40:26.761Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for the patch, that sounds like a good detail to clean up.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis sounds like a reasonable use case to extend this capability. It is partially redundant with the embedded shared memory transports provided by some of the middlewares, but this likely gives more control and potentially consistency but has tradeoffs such as limited QoS support.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf this makes sense for your use cases it would be great to see an implementation. I don’t think that anyone else has been working on it.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-08-11T16:40:26.761Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":51,"readers_count":50,"score":30.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":57240,"topic_slug":"has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored","display_username":"Tully Foote","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Great contributor","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":false,"staff":true,"user_id":3,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored/57240/5","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":116736,"name":"Daisuke Kato","username":"Daisuke_Kato","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/daisuke_kato/{size}/23487_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-12T04:48:15.852Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’m experimenting the shm backended buffer, combined with \u003ccode\u003ermw_fastrtps\u003c/code\u003epatches. To be honest, I’ve not read the whole code yet, and experimet results are a little bit messy, so it may take more time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox githubpullrequest\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/dskkato/memfd_buffer_backend/pull/1\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/dskkato/memfd_buffer_backend/pull/1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003egithub.com/dskkato/memfd_buffer_backend\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"github-row\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\"\u003e\n\n\n\n    \u003cdiv class=\"github-icon-container\" title=\"プルリクエスト\"\u003e\n      \u003csvg width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"github-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M11 11.28V5c-.03-.78-.34-1.47-.94-2.06C9.46 2.35 8.78 2.03 8 2H7V0L4 3l3 3V4h1c.27.02.48.11.69.31.21.2.3.42.31.69v6.28A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 10 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72zm-1 2.92c-.66 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2zM4 3c0-1.11-.89-2-2-2a1.993 1.993 0 0 0-1 3.72v6.56A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 2 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72V4.72c.59-.34 1-.98 1-1.72zm-.8 10c0 .66-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2-.65 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2zM2 4.2C1.34 4.2.8 3.65.8 3c0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"github-info-container\"\u003e\n\n\n\n      \u003ch4\u003e\n        \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/dskkato/memfd_buffer_backend/pull/1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eAdd memfd buffer backend implementation (#1)\u003c/a\u003e\n      \u003c/h4\u003e\n\n    \u003cdiv class=\"branches\"\u003e\n      \u003ccode\u003edevelop\u003c/code\u003e ← \u003ccode\u003ememfd-buffer-backend\u003c/code\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\n      \u003cdiv class=\"github-info\"\u003e\n        \u003cdiv class=\"date\"\u003e\n          オープン \u003cspan class=\"discourse-local-date\" data-format=\"ll\" data-date=\"2026-08-11\" data-time=\"22:59:19\" data-timezone=\"UTC\"\u003e10:59PM - 11 Aug 26 UTC\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n\n        \u003cdiv class=\"user\"\u003e\n          \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/dskkato\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\n            \u003cimg alt=\"\" src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/f/6/f6e0cc9bb89035f8a510335c29c5eeac271bcf06.jpeg\" class=\"onebox-avatar-inline\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" data-dominant-color=\"919471\"\u003e\n            dskkato\n          \u003c/a\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n\n        \u003cdiv class=\"lines\" title=\"7 個のコミットにより 24 個のファイルが変更されました。3282 個が追加され、12 個が削除されました。\"\u003e\n          \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/dskkato/memfd_buffer_backend/pull/1/files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"added\"\u003e+3282\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"removed\"\u003e-12\u003c/span\u003e\n          \u003c/a\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n      \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-08-12T04:48:15.852Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":48,"readers_count":47,"score":29.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":57240,"topic_slug":"has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored","display_username":"Daisuke Kato","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/dskkato/memfd_buffer_backend/pull/1","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Add memfd buffer backend implementation by dskkato · Pull Request #1 · dskkato/memfd_buffer_backend · GitHub","clicks":7}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":3,"username":"tfoote","name":"Tully Foote","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/tfoote/{size}/3813_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":29837,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored/57240/6","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":116855,"name":"Daisuke Kato","username":"Daisuke_Kato","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/daisuke_kato/{size}/23487_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-15T13:08:04.113Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eMy first implementation is now complete, and I believe anyone using Linux with ROS 2 Lyrical or later should be able to try it. The backend plugin is \u003ccode\u003ememfd\u003c/code\u003eaccording to \u003ccode\u003ememfd_create\u003c/code\u003e used to create sharable memory with a file descriptor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-116855-benchmark-results-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-116855-benchmark-results-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eBenchmark results\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI compared the latency of several backend and transport combinations using \u003ccode\u003esensor_msgs/Image\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003erosidl::Buffer\u003c/code\u003e backend\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003edefault CPU\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethis memfd backend\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003etransport setting\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003einter-process\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eintra-process\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis gives four configurations:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eInter CPU\u003c/strong\u003e — normal DDS communication\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eInter SHM\u003c/strong\u003e — the path introduced and optimized by this implementation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIntra CPU\u003c/strong\u003e — the ordinary optimized intra-process path\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIntra SHM\u003c/strong\u003e — the ordinary optimized intra-process path plus the buffer backend overhead\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLatency was measured:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003efrom immediately before \u003ccode\u003epublish()\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eto immediately after reading the first byte of the buffer\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere is the results of that combinations with various Payload from 64 B to 16 MiB.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere are the results for payload sizes ranging from 64 B to 16 MiB. The values are median / p99 latency in microseconds.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"md-table\"\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003ePayload\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eInter CPU\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eInter SHM\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eIntra CPU\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eIntra SHM\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e64 B\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e636.3 / 726.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e951.4 / 1,091.2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e144.5 / 179.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e114.8 / 173.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e641.5 / 719.7\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e942.3 / 1,060.1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e120.4 / 174.2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e115.7 / 162.4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e4 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e667.8 / 753.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e927.2 / 1,045.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e118.4 / 166.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e121.5 / 169.3\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e16 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e677.1 / 758.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e921.5 / 1,057.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e123.4 / 176.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e118.3 / 167.6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e64 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e687.6 / 776.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e958.8 / 1,107.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e124.6 / 174.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e123.1 / 168.2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e256 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1,009.1 / 1,153.5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1,033.0 / 1,128.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e113.8 / 138.6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e116.1 / 136.5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1 MiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e11,700.0 / 13,774.4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1,172.9 / 1,298.2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e118.4 / 128.7\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e119.8 / 132.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e4 MiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e15,407.8 / 16,025.3\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1,700.0 / 1,822.6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e108.2 / 117.2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e131.3 / 152.5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e16 MiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e14,879.5 / 16,019.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e2,289.5 / 2,718.5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e37.1 / 78.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e112.7 / 127.5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/c/6/c6dce68a5d1470a4642281b7053c17f6fbf93e6e.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/sndOCd32GnV4J2dBKCOmtZySTeu.png?dl=1\" title=\"baseline-path-latency\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/c/6/c6dce68a5d1470a4642281b7053c17f6fbf93e6e_2_690x404.png\" alt=\"baseline-path-latency\" data-base62-sha1=\"sndOCd32GnV4J2dBKCOmtZySTeu\" width=\"690\" height=\"404\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/c/6/c6dce68a5d1470a4642281b7053c17f6fbf93e6e_2_690x404.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/c/6/c6dce68a5d1470a4642281b7053c17f6fbf93e6e_2_1035x606.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/c/6/c6dce68a5d1470a4642281b7053c17f6fbf93e6e_2_1380x808.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F9F9F9\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003ebaseline-path-latency\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1960×1149 139 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen comparing the Inter CPU and Inter SHM results at small payload sizes, you may notice that Inter SHM has an additional overhead of about 300 microseconds. I suspect that this overhead mainly comes from creating the buffer descriptor from the buffer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Intra CPU and Intra SHM results support this interpretation: there is almost no difference between them, suggesting that using the SHM-backed buffer itself introduces very little overhead.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe latency of Inter SHM starts to increase above 256 KiB, even though the descriptor size remains almost constant. This was surprising, but I found that the increase came from the \u003ccode\u003ermw_fastrtps_cpp\u003c/code\u003e implementation, and I submitted a patch to address it:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox githubpullrequest\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003egithub.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"github-row\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\"\u003e\n\n\n\n    \u003cdiv class=\"github-icon-container\" title=\"プルリクエスト\"\u003e\n      \u003csvg width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"github-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M11 11.28V5c-.03-.78-.34-1.47-.94-2.06C9.46 2.35 8.78 2.03 8 2H7V0L4 3l3 3V4h1c.27.02.48.11.69.31.21.2.3.42.31.69v6.28A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 10 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72zm-1 2.92c-.66 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2zM4 3c0-1.11-.89-2-2-2a1.993 1.993 0 0 0-1 3.72v6.56A1.993 1.993 0 0 0 2 15a1.993 1.993 0 0 0 1-3.72V4.72c.59-.34 1-.98 1-1.72zm-.8 10c0 .66-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2-.65 0-1.2-.55-1.2-1.2 0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2zM2 4.2C1.34 4.2.8 3.65.8 3c0-.65.55-1.2 1.2-1.2.65 0 1.2.55 1.2 1.2 0 .65-.55 1.2-1.2 1.2z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"github-info-container\"\u003e\n\n\n\n      \u003ch4\u003e\n        \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eReuse FastBuffer managed buffer for each endpoint. (#904)\u003c/a\u003e\n      \u003c/h4\u003e\n\n    \u003cdiv class=\"branches\"\u003e\n      \u003ccode\u003erolling\u003c/code\u003e ← \u003ccode\u003edskkato:dskkato/reduce_extra_heap_allocations\u003c/code\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\n      \u003cdiv class=\"github-info\"\u003e\n        \u003cdiv class=\"date\"\u003e\n          オープン \u003cspan class=\"discourse-local-date\" data-format=\"ll\" data-date=\"2026-08-11\" data-time=\"08:24:48\" data-timezone=\"UTC\"\u003e08:24AM - 11 Aug 26 UTC\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n\n        \u003cdiv class=\"user\"\u003e\n          \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/dskkato\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\n            \u003cimg alt=\"\" src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/f/6/f6e0cc9bb89035f8a510335c29c5eeac271bcf06.jpeg\" class=\"onebox-avatar-inline\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" data-dominant-color=\"919471\"\u003e\n            dskkato\n          \u003c/a\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n\n        \u003cdiv class=\"lines\" title=\"1 個のコミットにより 1 個のファイルが変更されました。12 個が追加され、6 個が削除されました。\"\u003e\n          \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904/files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"added\"\u003e+12\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"removed\"\u003e-6\u003c/span\u003e\n          \u003c/a\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n      \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"github-row\"\u003e\n    \u003cp class=\"github-body-container\"\u003e## Description\n\nPreviously, heap allocation happend for each endpoint with std\u003cspan class=\"show-more-container\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\" class=\"show-more\"\u003e…\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"excerpt hidden\"\u003e::vector\u0026lt;uint8_t\u0026gt;. This introduced extra memset via its constructor.\n\nFor recent ROS 2, where rosidl::Buffer was introduced, sometimes the actual payload size and message size may not match because only buffer descriptors may be sent. In such a case, now `get_serialized_size()` seems to be unreliable, and hard to pre-allocate the buffer in that path.\n\nFixes #903\n\n### Is this user-facing behavior change?\n\n\n\nPossibly yes.\n\nPreviously, it is guaranteed that the heap allocation only happens once per endpoint, through externally managed buffer (allocated with `std::vector\u0026lt;uint8_t\u0026gt;`). Now the number of allocations depends on combinations of buffer's strategies, and Cdr's usage. So, in small message cases, this patch will introduce an extra overhead of buffer reallocation.\n\nFor rosidl::Buffer usage, this patch will dramatically reduce extra allocation and zero-initialization when only the optimized message paths exist. \n\n### Did you use Generative AI?\n\nI used CodeX to investigate the cause analysis, and FastBuffer/Cdr behavior.\n\n### Additional Information\n\nThis patch is trying to resolve two issues at same time:\n\n1. Reducing extra memory allocation when publishing rosidl::Buffer via optimized buf (carries only a descriptor) \n2. Removing extra memset caused by `std::vector\u0026lt;uint8_t\u0026gt;` constructor.\n\nWhat I originally found is the second point, so if we wish more conservative way, it is possible to reserve the `fast_buffer` as previouslly. Still, I believe it is better to reuse that buffer accross endpoints, in my perspective...\n\nSince this is my first PR to `rmw_fastrtps` repository, let me know if I missed anything.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIn my environment, the crossover point between Inter CPU and Inter SHM was around 256 KiB.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-116855-after-applying-the-patch-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-116855-after-applying-the-patch-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAfter applying the patch\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere are the results after applying the patch. In this case, the latency of Inter SHM remains almost constant.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is expected behavior: with a \u003ccode\u003ememfd\u003c/code\u003e-backed buffer, the payload itself does not need to be serialized, and the descriptor size is almost constant regardless of the payload size.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"md-table\"\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003ePayload\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eInter CPU\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eInter SHM\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eIntra CPU\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eIntra SHM\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e64 B\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e680.1 / 754.4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e944.0 / 1,073.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e120.7 / 174.7\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e118.2 / 160.4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e633.8 / 741.7\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e942.1 / 1,059.1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e121.1 / 171.6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e116.1 / 151.6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e4 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e666.1 / 752.3\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e956.8 / 1,071.7\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e115.9 / 169.6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e118.5 / 167.1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e16 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e701.8 / 792.3\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e936.0 / 1,044.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e153.8 / 190.3\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e116.7 / 150.6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e64 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e682.0 / 786.6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e925.1 / 1,091.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e115.3 / 177.4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e114.2 / 139.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e256 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1,076.0 / 1,139.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e937.4 / 1,054.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e114.6 / 136.5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e117.1 / 129.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1 MiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e13,005.8 / 13,638.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e935.6 / 1,050.5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e117.3 / 130.2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e120.9 / 133.2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e4 MiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e15,374.4 / 16,209.4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e915.6 / 1,049.2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e113.4 / 140.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e133.7 / 155.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e16 MiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e14,786.7 / 15,270.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e727.6 / 805.7\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e41.6 / 79.6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e113.3 / 124.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/4/4/4422513b005ed2ef93f33e3b78d00b447e5d4b28.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/9IJZx5WplHqyjU2dI3holCi6aaA.png?dl=1\" title=\"lazy-path-latency\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/4/4/4422513b005ed2ef93f33e3b78d00b447e5d4b28_2_690x404.png\" alt=\"lazy-path-latency\" data-base62-sha1=\"9IJZx5WplHqyjU2dI3holCi6aaA\" width=\"690\" height=\"404\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/4/4/4422513b005ed2ef93f33e3b78d00b447e5d4b28_2_690x404.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/4/4/4422513b005ed2ef93f33e3b78d00b447e5d4b28_2_1035x606.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/4/4/4422513b005ed2ef93f33e3b78d00b447e5d4b28_2_1380x808.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F9F9F9\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003elazy-path-latency\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1960×1149 151 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-116855-additional-notes-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-116855-additional-notes-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional notes\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou may also notice that Inter CPU, i.e. ordinary Fast DDS message passing, shows a significant latency increase around 1 MiB.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo investigate this, I compared the latency distributions of Inter CPU and Inter SHM. One notable difference is that the Inter CPU latency has a much wider, bimodal distribution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI have not yet investigated the exact cause in detail, but it may be related to the DDS configuration. For example, fragmentation of the DDS payload may occur for larger messages. If so, the behavior might be improved or stabilized by tuning the Fast DDS communication parameters.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn contrast, Inter SHM is much more stable. I believe this is because only a small descriptor is sent through DDS, rather than the actual payload. Since the descriptor is small enough to avoid the behavior seen with large DDS payloads, the pub/sub latency remains stable regardless of the actual payload size.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/original/3X/a/8/a8cd6b80b0250a4b4c2fb5d79b114601c6bd368f.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/o5ika6PQiEhYYcufrDLbuQiyO51.png?dl=1\" title=\"1m-baseline-inter-latency-distribution\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/a/8/a8cd6b80b0250a4b4c2fb5d79b114601c6bd368f_2_690x445.png\" alt=\"1m-baseline-inter-latency-distribution\" data-base62-sha1=\"o5ika6PQiEhYYcufrDLbuQiyO51\" width=\"690\" height=\"445\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/a/8/a8cd6b80b0250a4b4c2fb5d79b114601c6bd368f_2_690x445.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/a/8/a8cd6b80b0250a4b4c2fb5d79b114601c6bd368f_2_1035x667.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex022/uploads/ros/optimized/3X/a/8/a8cd6b80b0250a4b4c2fb5d79b114601c6bd368f_2_1380x890.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F8F8F9\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003e1m-baseline-inter-latency-distribution\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1870×1207 89.1 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-116855-whats-next-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-116855-whats-next-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat’s next?\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe implementation is almost complete, so I do not currently have a specific roadmap for this plugin.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, if you try it and find any issues, I would be very happy to investigate them. Feedback is always welcome.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-08-15T13:08:04.113Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":40,"readers_count":39,"score":148.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":57240,"topic_slug":"has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored","display_username":"Daisuke Kato","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/ros2/rmw_fastrtps/pull/904","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Reuse FastBuffer managed buffer for each endpoint. by dskkato · Pull Request #904 · ros2/rmw_fastrtps · GitHub","clicks":3}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":4}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":29837,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored/57240/7","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":4}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":4,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":116857,"name":"Michael Carroll","username":"mjcarroll","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/mjcarroll/{size}/658_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-15T15:06:27.493Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAmazing, thanks for the effort here, I’m excited to see where this is headed!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCC: \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/jm_ros\"\u003e@JM_ROS\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/skye.galaxy\"\u003e@skye.galaxy\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/alsora\"\u003e@alsora\u003c/a\u003e from a client library perspective\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-08-15T15:06:27.493Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":34,"readers_count":33,"score":41.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":57240,"topic_slug":"has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored","display_username":"Michael Carroll","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"OSRA TGC Member","title_is_group":false,"reply_to_user":{"id":29837,"username":"Daisuke_Kato","name":"Daisuke Kato","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/daisuke_kato/{size}/23487_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":true,"admin":false,"staff":true,"user_id":1095,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[{"id":22772,"username":"JM_ROS","name":"","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/jm_ros/{size}/12964_2.png"},{"id":30529,"username":"skye.galaxy","name":"Skyler Medeiros","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/skye.galaxy/{size}/30716_2.png"},{"id":14357,"username":"alsora","name":"Alberto Soragna","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/alsora/{size}/2514_2.png"}],"post_url":"/t/has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored/57240/8","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":116860,"name":"Martin Pecka","username":"peci1","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/peci1/{size}/10145_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-15T15:27:10.721Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThis is awesome! Thanks for the implementation and tests!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDo you have an explanation for the latency drop at 16 MiB for Intra CPU?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-08-15T15:27:10.721Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":34,"readers_count":33,"score":16.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":57240,"topic_slug":"has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored","display_username":"Martin Pecka","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Great contributor","title_is_group":false,"reply_to_user":{"id":29837,"username":"Daisuke_Kato","name":"Daisuke Kato","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/daisuke_kato/{size}/23487_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":5103,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"user_status":{"description":"Czech Technical University in Prague","emoji":"czechia","ends_at":null,"message_bus_last_id":0},"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored/57240/9","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":116862,"name":"Daisuke Kato","username":"Daisuke_Kato","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/daisuke_kato/{size}/23487_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-15T22:14:51.379Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eMy guess is that this is a benchmark artifact rather than a real 16 MiB optimization.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince the drop appears only with the CPU backend, I suspect some size-dependent behavior in the normal buffer allocation/lifecycle, possibly in the allocator or below \u003ccode\u003erclcpp\u003c/code\u003e/\u003ccode\u003ermw\u003c/code\u003e. Repeating the same simple benchmark may also make allocation and memory reuse unusually favorable. I haven’t verified which effect is dominant yet.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":10,"post_type":1,"posts_count":11,"updated_at":"2026-08-15T22:14:51.379Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":9,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":34,"readers_count":33,"score":16.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":57240,"topic_slug":"has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored","display_username":"Daisuke Kato","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":5103,"username":"peci1","name":"Martin Pecka","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/peci1/{size}/10145_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":29837,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/has-a-cpu-shared-memory-backend-for-rosidl-buffer-been-explored/57240/10","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false},{"id":117143,"name":"Daisuke Kato","username":"Daisuke_Kato","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.openrobotics.org/daisuke_kato/{size}/23487_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-22T07:34:46.332Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI noticed that \u003ccode\u003ermw_zenoh\u003c/code\u003e also added \u003ccode\u003erosidl::Buffer\u003c/code\u003e support to lyrical branch, and the change was released in September.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe latency trend for memfd-based inter-process communication looks almost identical to \u003ccode\u003ermw_fastrtps\u003c/code\u003e, so I think \u003ccode\u003ermw_zenoh\u003c/code\u003eis ready to try, not only with memfd but also with the CUDAbackend.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"md-table\"\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003ePayload\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003efastrtps lazy\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003ezenoh\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth style=\"text-align:right\"\u003eZenoh p50 change\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e64 B\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e944.0 / 1,073.8\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e949.7 / 1,077.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e+0.6%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e1 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e942.1 / 1,059.1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e951.7 / 1,127.9\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e+1.0%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e4 KiB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e956.8 / 1,071.7\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e953.6 / 1,070.5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd style=\"text-align:right\"\u003e-0.3%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003